    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A task card and an experienced volunteer are available for each routine garden activity.\", \"decision\": \"How should an unfamiliar volunteer learn a routine task?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe newcomer and experienced volunteer follow the task card together for the first attempt. Questions can be resolved at the moment each instruction is used.\nThe newcomer reads the task card, tries the activity, and then asks the experienced volunteer to check. Practice begins independently with a later correction opportunity.\nThe experienced volunteer demonstrates the activity before the newcomer follows the task card. The written instructions are connected to an observed example."
    }
